<title>USA: CME May volume rises 15.3 pct year-on-year.</title>
<headline>CME May volume rises 15.3 pct year-on-year.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Chicago Mercantile Exchange (CME) said volume in its futures and options totaled 18,631,157 contracts in May, up 15.3 percent from 16,164,241 contracts a year earlier.</p>
<p>Open interest at the end of the month stood at 7,434,315 contracts, up 6.6 percent from 6,975,479 at the end of May last year.</p>
<p>Year-to-date volume through May totaled 91,409,099 contracts, up 7.4 percent from 85,090,369 during the same period in 1996.  </p>
<p>Major categories and volumes were as follows:</p>
<p>Futures (individual)    May 1997    % change	   May 1996</p>
<p>  Eurodollar	     9,403,779	 +16.0	  8,109,916</p>
<p>  Deutschemark	     471,348	 - 5.1	    496,654</p>
<p>  Japanese yen	     604,616	 +37.9	    438,466</p>
<p>  Swiss franc		432,532	 +31.4	    329,126</p>
<p>  British pound	    236,648	 -25.2	    316,413</p>
<p>  Canadian dollar	     230,733	 +54.7	    149,188</p>
<p>  S&amp;P 500		  1,601,564	 - 7.3	  1,727,965</p>
<p>  Live cattle		285,913	 -25.9	    385,936</p>
<p>  Lean hogs		  222,877	 + 5.9	    210,558</p>
<p>Options on futures</p>
<p>  Eurodollar	   2,071,228	  +39.3	   1,486,861</p>
<p>  Eurodollar midcurve     879,139	 +126.0	     388,952</p>
<p>  Deutschemark	   120,664	  -32.7	     179,412</p>
<p>  Japanese yen	   197,251	  - 9.8	     218,570</p>
<p>  British pound	  248,872	  -47.2	     471,424</p>
<p>  S&amp;P 500		  534,586	  +13.8	     469,644</p>
<p>  Live cattle	     43,889	  -20.9		55,481</p>
<p>  Hogs			14,601	  -31.9		21,446</p>
<p>Since January 1994 CME has counted in volume anything that creates or liquidates open positions including expired options and SIMEX mutual offset transactions cleared on the CME.</p>
<p>Excluding these transactions, CME &quot;pit traded&quot; volume for May totaled 16,925,982 and year-to-date volume totaled 82,774,588.</p>
<p>-- Chicago Derivatives Desk ((312-408-8750))</p>
